    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d366-a1">

                <pb facs="0648" n="514" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg514"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 302.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Stewart to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >United States Senate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Washington,
                                D. C.</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1888-02-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 18, 1888</date>. (Received February
                    20.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Inclosed find letter from the governor of
                    Nevada, C. C. Stevenson, in regard to John Fruchier, an American citizen, who
                    was pressed into the military service of France some fourteen months ago while
                    on a visit to relatives. It seems to me to be a matter requiring the attention
                    of your Department. Please inform me what has been done in the matter.</p>
                <p>Yours, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. M.
                            Stewart.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
